# Snyk's IntelliJ plugin auto-ran its project scan the moment a project is
# opened: SnykTaskQueueService.scan() queues a Task.Backgroundable whose run()
# body saves the documents and then unconditionally fans out into
# scheduleSnykCodeScan / scheduleOssScan / scheduleIacScan / scheduleContainerScan.
# Those scans drive the Snyk CLI over the opened project, and analyzing a
# project executes the project's own build tooling and metadata files, so a
# user who clones a malicious repository gets code execution the moment the IDE
# opens it (CWE-78 / CWE-94 as recorded by the advisory; the injection itself
# lives in the snyk CLI npm package, this repository's share of the defect is
# that the scan is launched with no notion of whether the project is trusted).
#
# The fixed revision (56682f4b, GHSA-4vrv-93c7-m92j) adds a workspace-trust gate at the
# very top of run():
#     project.basePath?.let {
#         if (!confirmScanningAndSetWorkspaceTrustedStateIfNeeded(Paths.get(it))) return
#     }
# backed by three new files in a private snyk.trust package: a
# WorkspaceTrustSettings persistent component holding a trusted-path list, a
# WorkspaceTrustService consulting it, and TrustedProjects.kt showing a modal
# MessageDialogBuilder.yesNo dialog and recording the answer.
#
# ATTENTION, rechecked. Nothing here is a dataflow defect and nothing in the
# remediation is nameable through a documented API, so no binding separates the
# two revisions. Measured on the real checkout, three --cache off runs per
# side, stable:
#   * `vyql match` on SnykTaskQueueService.kt labels nothing at either
#     revision -- no source, no sink, no control. project.basePath is the IDE's
#     own configuration, not attacker text, and the fan-out calls are the
#     plugin's own private methods.
#   * The whole repository scans to 12 findings at 56682f4b^ and a
#     byte-identical 12 at 56682f4b -- same rules, same finding fingerprints,
#     over three runs each. Eleven sit on test fixtures
#     (kubernetes-deployment.yaml, terraform-main.tf, package.json,
#     requirements.txt, ConsoleCommandRunnerTest.kt). The one finding in
#     src/main is VYQL-CFG-004 code.CertValidationDisabled on the CLI
#     downloader's NoopHostnameVerifier
#     (services/download/HttpRequestHelper.kt:12) -- a real but separate
#     weakness in the same plugin, carried identically by both revisions, so
#     it is not coverage of this one.
#   * The review-flag view agrees: 10 flags at 56682f4b^ against 11 at
#     56682f4b, the only difference a core.ResourceRelease control on the fix's
#     own new test helper (src/test/kotlin/snyk/InMemoryFsRule.kt:30). A
#     control, not a detection -- `-flag-loc trust` returns no flags at all on
#     the fixed revision, so nothing labels the trust package the fix adds.
#   * The counterweight test fails. The new trust files import only generic
#     IntelliJ platform APIs -- MessageDialogBuilder, Messages,
#     SimplePersistentStateComponent, @Service, Logger -- plus java.nio.file.
#     Across every clone under /tmp/cve-work, MessageDialogBuilder appears in
#     exactly one Kotlin file, TrustedProjects.kt, the fixed revision itself,
#     so a binding keyed on it is keyed on the fixing commit's own vocabulary:
#     renaming the helper it sits behind loses the flag entirely. basePath,
#     the other candidate, appears in 22 Kotlin files across the same corpus
#     and is semantically just "where the project lives".
#   * The gate is not nameable where it stands anyway. `vyql graph` on the
#     fixed service file lowers `project.basePath?.let` as a call named
#     project.basePath.let, while the negated
#     `!confirmScanningAndSetWorkspaceTrustedStateIfNeeded(Paths.get(it))` on
#     the next line yields no call node carrying the helper's name at all:
#     tree-sitter-kotlin parses `!guard(it)` as a call_expression whose callee
#     is a unary_expression, and ktConv.dotted
#     (internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/kotlin.go:710) has no case for
#     that kind, so the call lowers with Path "?". That is the callee-side
#     face of the engine gap recorded against rank 1214, and it is open even
#     though the argument-side half is fixed. Closing it would make the
#     helper's own name reachable -- and that name is precisely what a
#     binding must not key on.
#   * The fix consults no documented IntelliJ trust API anywhere: it rolls its
#     own dialog over MessageDialogBuilder and its own allowlist over
#     SimplePersistentStateComponent. So the "did the fix leave a documented
#     API call inside the method it guards" test fails, and the shape reduces
#     to a scan handler with no authorization signal in its body -- the
#     measured-unshippable family, every variant of which scores identically
#     on the vulnerable and the patched tree because the control lands in
#     named helpers and framework hooks.
#
# The spec pins the miss: neither revision of the auto-scan may fire the
# command-injection rule of the advisory's own class, the trust-boundary
# misconfig rule, or the missing-authentication rule. Nothing is `expect`ed,
# because nothing is labelled -- a positive assertion here would fail rather
# than document.

test "rank1767: the auto-scan launched on project open, with no trust gate"
  lang kotlin
  file src/main/kotlin/io/snyk/plugin/services/SnykTaskQueueService.kt
  reject VYQL-INJ-002
  reject VYQL-CFG-014
  reject VYQL-AUTH-001
  code
  ```
  package io.snyk.plugin.services

  import com.intellij.openapi.application.ApplicationManager
  import com.intellij.openapi.components.Service
  import com.intellij.openapi.fileEditor.FileDocumentManager
  import com.intellij.openapi.progress.BackgroundTaskQueue
  import com.intellij.openapi.progress.ProgressIndicator
  import com.intellij.openapi.progress.Task
  import com.intellij.openapi.project.Project
  import io.snyk.plugin.getSnykCachedResults
  import io.snyk.plugin.isIacEnabled
  import io.snyk.plugin.isContainerEnabled
  import io.snyk.plugin.pluginSettings

  @Service
  class SnykTaskQueueService(val project: Project) {
      private val taskQueue = BackgroundTaskQueue(project, "Snyk")
      private val taskQueueIac = BackgroundTaskQueue(project, "Snyk: Iac")
      private val taskQueueContainer = BackgroundTaskQueue(project, "Snyk: Container")

      private val settings
          get() = pluginSettings()

      fun scan() {
          taskQueue.run(object : Task.Backgroundable(project, "Snyk wait for changed files to be saved on disk", true) {
              override fun run(indicator: ProgressIndicator) {
                  ApplicationManager.getApplication().invokeAndWait {
                      FileDocumentManager.getInstance().saveAllDocuments()
                  }
                  indicator.checkCanceled()

                  if (settings.snykCodeSecurityIssuesScanEnable || settings.snykCodeQualityIssuesScanEnable) {
                      scheduleSnykCodeScan()
                  }

                  waitUntilCliDownloadedIfNeeded(indicator)
                  indicator.checkCanceled()

                  if (settings.ossScanEnable) {
                      scheduleOssScan()
                  }
                  if (isIacEnabled() && settings.iacScanEnabled) {
                      scheduleIacScan()
                  }
                  if (isContainerEnabled() && settings.containerScanEnabled) {
                      scheduleContainerScan()
                  }
              }
          })
      }

      private fun waitUntilCliDownloadedIfNeeded(indicator: ProgressIndicator) {
          if (!isCliInstalled()) return
          Thread.sleep(waitForDownloadMillis)
      }

      private fun scheduleOssScan() {
          taskQueue.run(object : Task.Backgroundable(project, "Snyk is running...", true) {
              override fun run(indicator: ProgressIndicator) {
                  val cliAdapter = CliAdapter(project)
                  cliAdapter.scan()
              }
          })
      }

      private fun scheduleIacScan() {
          taskQueueIac.run(object : Task.Backgroundable(project, "Snyk IaC is scanning...", true) {
              override fun run(indicator: ProgressIndicator) {
                  val iacService = getIacService(project)
                  iacService?.scan()
              }
          })
      }

      private fun scheduleContainerScan() {
          taskQueueContainer.run(object : Task.Backgroundable(project, "Snyk Container is scanning...", true) {
              override fun run(indicator: ProgressIndicator) {
                  val containerResult = getContainerService(project)?.scan()
              }
          })
      }

      private fun scheduleSnykCodeScan() {}
      private fun isCliInstalled() = true
      private fun getIacService(project: Project) = null
      private fun getContainerService(project: Project) = null

      companion object {
          var waitForDownloadMillis = 100L
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1767: the trust gate added at the top of the auto-scan body"
  lang kotlin
  file src/main/kotlin/io/snyk/plugin/services/SnykTaskQueueService.kt
  reject VYQL-INJ-002
  reject VYQL-CFG-014
  reject VYQL-AUTH-001
  code
  ```
  package io.snyk.plugin.services

  import com.intellij.openapi.application.ApplicationManager
  import com.intellij.openapi.components.Service
  import com.intellij.openapi.fileEditor.FileDocumentManager
  import com.intellij.openapi.progress.BackgroundTaskQueue
  import com.intellij.openapi.progress.ProgressIndicator
  import com.intellij.openapi.progress.Task
  import com.intellij.openapi.project.Project
  import io.snyk.plugin.pluginSettings
  import io.snyk.plugin.isIacEnabled
  import io.snyk.plugin.isContainerEnabled
  import snyk.trust.confirmScanningAndSetWorkspaceTrustedStateIfNeeded
  import java.nio.file.Paths

  @Service
  class SnykTaskQueueService(val project: Project) {
      private val taskQueue = BackgroundTaskQueue(project, "Snyk")
      private val taskQueueIac = BackgroundTaskQueue(project, "Snyk: Iac")
      private val taskQueueContainer = BackgroundTaskQueue(project, "Snyk: Container")

      private val settings
          get() = pluginSettings()

      fun scan() {
          taskQueue.run(object : Task.Backgroundable(project, "Snyk wait for changed files to be saved on disk", true) {
              override fun run(indicator: ProgressIndicator) {
                  project.basePath?.let {
                      if (!confirmScanningAndSetWorkspaceTrustedStateIfNeeded(Paths.get(it))) return
                  }

                  ApplicationManager.getApplication().invokeAndWait {
                      FileDocumentManager.getInstance().saveAllDocuments()
                  }
                  indicator.checkCanceled()

                  if (settings.snykCodeSecurityIssuesScanEnable || settings.snykCodeQualityIssuesScanEnable) {
                      scheduleSnykCodeScan()
                  }

                  waitUntilCliDownloadedIfNeeded(indicator)
                  indicator.checkCanceled()

                  if (settings.ossScanEnable) {
                      scheduleOssScan()
                  }
                  if (isIacEnabled() && settings.iacScanEnabled) {
                      scheduleIacScan()
                  }
              }
          })
      }

      private fun waitUntilCliDownloadedIfNeeded(indicator: ProgressIndicator) {
          if (!isCliInstalled()) return
          Thread.sleep(waitForDownloadMillis)
      }

      private fun scheduleOssScan() {
          taskQueue.run(object : Task.Backgroundable(project, "Snyk is running...", true) {
              override fun run(indicator: ProgressIndicator) {
                  val cliAdapter = CliAdapter(project)
                  cliAdapter.scan()
              }
          })
      }

      private fun scheduleIacScan() {}
      private fun scheduleSnykCodeScan() {}
      private fun isCliInstalled() = true

      companion object {
          var waitForDownloadMillis = 100L
      }
  }
  ```
